import Mathlib
import InverseGalois.Solvable.Shafarevich.LevelRepair
import InverseGalois.Solvable.Shafarevich.RamifiedSplit

/-!
# The repair, read prime by prime

What the arithmetic owes the ladder is a lift carrying the restriction on ramification.  The
restriction quantifies over the primes at which the lift ramifies over the base realization, and
those primes fall into three kinds according to how the solution one level below behaves at them.

At a prime where the solution below already ramifies over the base realization, the solution below
carries the restriction, so the base realization splits completely there and what is asked of the
lift is a statement about its own local image; there is nothing to be gained by rephrasing it and
it is asked as it stands.  At a prime where the solution below does not ramify over the base
realization but does not split completely either, the restriction cannot be met if the lift ramifies
at all, so what is asked is that it not: the new ramification has to avoid such primes.  At a prime
where the solution below splits completely, the values of the lift on the decomposition subgroup
come from the layer and are killed by the prime, the base realization kills the decomposition
subgroup, and the remaining clauses of the restriction reduce to a single one — that the local image
be cyclic.

So the repair is asked in the form the class field theory can answer: **produce a lift whose new
ramification is confined to the primes at which the solution below splits completely, and is cyclic
there.**

## Main definitions

* `InverseGalois.Shafarevich.HasCyclicRepair` — **the repair, read prime by prime**.

## Main results

* `InverseGalois.Shafarevich.hasLiftRepair_of_hasCyclicRepair` — **the three clauses read prime by
  prime are the repair**, for a base realization fixing the roots of unity of order the square of
  the prime.

## Tags

Shafarevich's theorem, embedding problem, ramification, cyclic extension, decomposition group
-/

namespace InverseGalois.Shafarevich

open MulAction NumberField

open InverseGalois.CFT

open scoped Pointwise

variable (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime] (U : Type) [Group U] [Finite U] (n : ℕ) (S : Type) [Group S]
  [Finite S] (j : ℕ) {k Ω : Type*} [Field k] [Field Ω] [Algebra k Ω] (φ : Gal(Ω/k) →* U) {t : ℕ}
  (D : Fin t → Subgroup Gal(Ω/k))

/-! ### The repair, prime by prime -/

/-- **The repair, read prime by prime.**

The data is that of `InverseGalois.Shafarevich.HasLiftRepair`: a solution at one rung carrying the
restriction, and a lift of it across the next layer which is smooth, over that solution and trivial
on the part of each member of the finite family the base realization already kills.  What is asked
back is another such lift, subject to three conditions read off one prime at a time.

At a prime where the solution below ramifies over the base realization, the lift is asked to carry
the restriction outright.  At a prime where the solution below does not ramify over the base
realization but does not split completely there, the lift is asked not to ramify over the base
realization either.  At a prime where the solution below splits completely, the image of the
decomposition subgroup under the lift is asked to be cyclic, generated by one of its own values. -/
def HasCyclicRepair : Prop :=
  ∀ (Φ : Gal(Ω/k) →* GenericQuot ℓ U n S j) (f : Gal(Ω/k) →* GenericQuot ℓ U n S (j + 1)),
    IsSmoothHom Φ → (∀ x, SemidirectProduct.rightHom (Φ x) = φ x) →
    IsSplitTotallyRamifiedHom ℓ φ Φ → IsSmoothHom f →
    (∀ x, (layerExtension ℓ (genericAut U n S) j).rightHom (f x) = Φ x) →
    (∀ ν : Fin t, ∀ x ∈ D ν, φ x = 1 → f x = 1) →
    ∃ Ψ : Gal(Ω/k) →* GenericQuot ℓ U n S (j + 1), IsSmoothHom Ψ ∧
      (∀ x, (layerExtension ℓ (genericAut U n S) j).rightHom (Ψ x) = Φ x) ∧
      (∀ ν : Fin t, ∀ x ∈ D ν, φ x = 1 → Ψ x = 1) ∧
      (∀ Q : Ideal (𝓞 Ω), Q.IsPrime → Q ≠ ⊥ →
        (∃ x ∈ Ideal.inertia Gal(Ω/k) Q, φ x = 1 ∧ Φ x ≠ 1) →
          IsSplitTotallyRamifiedAt ℓ φ Ψ Q) ∧
      (∀ Q : Ideal (𝓞 Ω), Q.IsPrime → Q ≠ ⊥ →
        (∀ x ∈ Ideal.inertia Gal(Ω/k) Q, φ x = 1 → Φ x = 1) →
          (∃ x ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q, Φ x ≠ 1) →
            ∀ x ∈ Ideal.inertia Gal(Ω/k) Q, φ x = 1 → Ψ x = 1) ∧
      ∀ Q : Ideal (𝓞 Ω), Q.IsPrime → Q ≠ ⊥ → (∀ x ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q, Φ x = 1) →
        ∃ x₀ ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q,
          ∀ x ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q, Ψ x ∈ Subgroup.zpowers (Ψ x₀)

/-! ### The three clauses are the repair -/

variable {ℓ U n S j φ D}

/-- **The three clauses read prime by prime are the repair**, for a base realization fixing the
roots of unity of order the square of the prime.

A prime at which the produced lift ramifies over the base realization is of one of three kinds.  If
the solution below ramifies there the first clause carries the restriction.  If it does not, and
does not split completely there either, the second clause says the produced lift does not ramify
there, which the prime was chosen to contradict.  If it splits completely there, the third clause
makes the local image cyclic, and cyclicity is the whole of what is left of the restriction at such
a prime. -/
theorem hasLiftRepair_of_hasCyclicRepair
    (hmu : ∀ ζ : Ωˣ, ζ ^ (ℓ * ℓ) = 1 → ∀ σ ∈ φ.ker, σ • ζ = ζ)
    (h : HasCyclicRepair ℓ U n S j φ D) : HasLiftRepair ℓ U n S j φ D := by
  intro Φ f hΦsm hΦright hΦP _ hfsm hfright hfD
  obtain ⟨Ψ, hΨsm, hΨright, hΨD, hold, hmid, hnew⟩ :=
    h Φ f hΦsm hΦright hΦP hfsm hfright hfD
  refine ⟨Ψ, hΨsm, hΨright, hΨD, fun Q hQp hQbot hram => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨x, hxI, hxφ, hxΨ⟩ := hram
  by_cases hΦram : ∃ x ∈ Ideal.inertia Gal(Ω/k) Q, φ x = 1 ∧ Φ x ≠ 1
  · exact hold Q hQp hQbot hΦram
  · have hunr : ∀ y ∈ Ideal.inertia Gal(Ω/k) Q, φ y = 1 → Φ y = 1 := by
      intro y hy hyφ
      by_contra hy1
      exact hΦram ⟨y, hy, hyφ, hy1⟩
    by_cases hsplit : ∃ y ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q, Φ y ≠ 1
    · exact absurd (hmid Q hQp hQbot hunr hsplit x hxI hxφ) hxΨ
    · have hΦ0 : ∀ y ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/k) Q, Φ y = 1 := by
        intro y hy
        by_contra hy1
        exact hsplit ⟨y, hy, hy1⟩
      exact isSplitTotallyRamifiedAt_of_zpowers_of_rightHom hΦright hΨright hΦ0
        (hnew Q hQp hQbot hΦ0) ⟨x, hxI, hxΨ⟩ hmu

end InverseGalois.Shafarevich
